From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flax <flax@tiogapass>
Date: Thu, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] event log: show AdditionalData inline on row expand

Event log entries that carry AdditionalData (for example a
CriticalServiceFailure, whose attachment holds SYSTEMD_UNIT and
SYSTEMD_RESULT) previously only offered a download button - the detail
that makes the entry meaningful was never displayed.

Add a store action that fetches the entry's AdditionalData attachment
(bmcweb returns it as a { key: value } JSON object) and render those
key/value pairs inline in the expandable row details.  The fetch is
lazy (on expand) and cached per entry, so it adds no cost to the log
listing.  This is generic: any source that attaches AdditionalData now
shows its detail, not just CriticalServiceFailure.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/store/modules/Logs/EventLogStore.js |  12 ++
 src/views/Logs/EventLogs/EventLogs.vue  |  35 ++++
 2 files changed, 47 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/store/modules/Logs/EventLogStore.js b/src/store/modules/Logs/EventLogStore.js
index 1111111..2222222 100644
@@ -239,6 +239,18 @@
           );
         });
     },
+    // Fetch the AdditionalData attachment for an entry and return it as a
+    // plain { key: value } object (e.g. { SYSTEMD_UNIT: '...' }) so the detail
+    // can be shown inline instead of only being downloadable.
+    async getEntryAdditionalData(_, uri) {
+      return await api
+        .get(uri)
+        .then(({ data }) => data)
+        .catch((error) => {
+          console.log(error);
+          return null;
+        });
+    },
   },
 };
 
diff --git a/src/views/Logs/EventLogs/EventLogs.vue b/src/views/Logs/EventLogs/EventLogs.vue
index 3333333..4444444 100644
@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@
               :aria-label="expandRowLabel"
               :title="expandRowLabel"
